cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this protocol, screening database, extraction database, or evidence map, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
title: "The Legal Last Mile: An AI-Assisted Systematic Review of Legal and Administrative Barriers to Water and Sanitation Access — Protocol, Screening Database, and Evidence Base (Interim)"
abstract: >
  Companion systematic review to the doctoral dissertation "The Legal Last
  Mile: Administrative Law as a Mechanism of Connectivity and Exclusion in
  Sanitation Governance." Pre-specified protocol, inclusion/exclusion
  criteria, and extraction codebook (fixed 2026-08-22, before any database
  was searched), plus the review's title/abstract screening database
  (27,481 deduplicated candidate records from Scopus, Web of Science,
  HeinOnline, ProQuest, ProQuest/Sociological Abstracts, and JSTOR),
  full-text screening database, 92-field extraction database, evidence
  classification map, rule-based risk-of-bias appraisals, effect-size table,
  and three structured (SWiM) syntheses with a sensitivity analysis. This is
  an INTERIM deposit (release 0.2.0-interim, 2026-10-14): searching and
  full-text retrieval were closed by researcher decision on 2026-09-28,
  1,080 included reports (1,078 distinct studies) were extracted and
  appraised, and no effect could be pooled. Screening, extraction, appraisal
  and synthesis were carried out by an AI under the researcher's direction
  and are only partly human-verified, and the protocol was not registered
  before the work was done -- see PRISMA_WORKFLOW.md, README.md, and
  00_admin/DECISIONS_AND_OPEN_ITEMS.md in this deposit for the disclosed
  status of every phase. Never treat any count or figure here as final;
  re-check the source CSVs and the changelog for the version actually cited.
authors:
